static const char _zs232_d[] = "reserved member name\n\nA type body declares a member named `lock`, `take`, `borrow`, `drop`, `private` or `public`. These are ownership/access markers in member position and cannot be declared. Rename the member; the visibility declarations `public:`/`private:` naming a unit block remain valid.";
static const z_t78_t _zs232 = { .data = _zs232_d, .size = 294 };
static const char _zs233_d[] = "malformed require block\n\nA unit's `require:` block declares what the unit needs from the host toolchain. It must be a unit definition, must declare at least one requirement, and every entry must be a key the compiler consumes -- today only `library:`, whose value is a plain string literal naming a link library. An unknown or misspelt key would be silently ignored, so it is rejected.";
static const z_t78_t _zs233 = { .data = _zs233_d, .size = 385 };
static const char _zs234_d[] = "no main\n\nThe unit being compiled declares no `main: function is { ... }`, so the compiler has no entry point to start from. Compilation is demand-driven: `main` is the root, and what it reaches is what gets checked and emitted. A unit with no `main` is a library -- compile the program that opens it instead, or add a `main`. `--eager` resolves every definition rather than what a root reaches, so it does not require one.";
static const z_t78_t _zs234 = { .data = _zs234_d, .size = 422 };
static const char _zs235_d[] = "type error\n\nA value's type does not match what is required here: a mismatch, an undefined type, or an incompatible assignment.";
static const z_t78_t _zs235 = { .data = _zs235_d, .size = 126 };
static const char _zs236_d[] = "member not public\n\nThe member exists but is not in the type's `public:` interface. Access it from within the type's own methods (`this`), or through a `.private` friend handle the type handed out.";
static const z_t78_t _zs236 = { .data = _zs236_d, .size = 196 };
static const char _zs237_d[] = "private escape\n\nA `.private` view may only be taken by the value's own type, or by a holder of an existing `.private` handle (a friend the type passed it to). External code holding only a public value cannot produce one.";
static const z_t78_t _zs237 = { .data = _zs237_d, .size = 220 };
static const char _zs238_d[] = "ownership error\n\nA value's ownership was used incorrectly: used after a take/move, a borrow outliving its lock, or a reftype aliased while locked. See docs/ownership.";
static const z_t78_t _zs238 = { .data = _zs238_d, .size = 166 };
static const char _zs239_d[] = "call error\n\nA call's arguments do not match the callee: wrong count, an unknown named argument, or an argument type mismatch. Also raised for a bare type name in value position that cannot construct its zero value: required fields missing, or a family with no zero-argument create (unions/variants select an arm, views bind from an owner, generic templates need type arguments).";
